WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.167
This is CtxVault:

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.020
local memory for AI agents.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.765
Every vault is a folder on your machine,

00:00:05.765 --> 00:00:08.305
with a type, and a list of the agents

00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:09.540
that can reach it.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.999
Semantic vaults hold documents,

00:00:12.999 --> 00:00:14.203
searched by meaning.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.786
Skill vaults hold procedures:

00:00:17.786 --> 00:00:19.530
how an agent should do things.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.374
Episodic vaults hold episodes:

00:00:23.374 --> 00:00:25.573
facts, and when each one was true.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.083
And every agent reaches only

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.757
the vaults it has been given.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.491
Open a vault, and you see where it lives on disk:

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:37.219
a plain folder you can open,

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:38.268
edit and back up,

00:00:38.268 --> 00:00:39.997
and how much space it takes.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.848
A semantic vault shows its documents,

00:00:42.848 --> 00:00:45.460
and the chunks the agent actually receives.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.139
And you can search it the way the agent does:

00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:49.792
by meaning,

00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:52.167
with a similarity score for every match.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.711
A skill vault holds procedures

00:00:55.711 --> 00:00:56.940
written in markdown.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.276
Each one has a name and a description,

00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:01.489
so the agent can pick the right one,

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:03.087
and then follow its steps.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.056
An episodic vault shows

00:01:06.056 --> 00:01:07.702
which episodes hold today:

00:01:07.702 --> 00:01:10.298
what changed recently, what is coming up,

00:01:10.298 --> 00:01:12.260
and where two sources disagree.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.433
Every episode keeps its history:

00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:16.089
when it was true in the world,

00:01:16.089 --> 00:01:18.297
and when the episodic memory learned it.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.304
And you can rewind it.

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:23.726
Drag back in time to see

00:01:23.726 --> 00:01:26.215
which episodes were true on any given day,

00:01:26.215 --> 00:01:28.171
and what the episodic memory knew

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:29.060
at that moment.
